@as6o That's true !
Easy fix from outside is to remove in the meantime any '=' from boundary.

On fix part on Netty, that should be done for instance this way:
Change

```
        String[] boundary = StringUtil.split(headerContentType[1], '=');
        if (boundary.length != 2) {
            throw new ErrorDataDecoderException("Needs a boundary value");
        }
        if (boundary[1].charAt(0) == '"') {
            String bound = boundary[1].trim();
            int index = bound.length() - 1;
            if (bound.charAt(index) == '"') {
                boundary[1] = bound.substring(1, index);
            }
        }
        multipartDataBoundary = "--" + boundary[1];
```

By

```
        int pos = headerContentType[1].indexOf('=');
        if (pos <= 0) {
            throw new ErrorDataDecoderException("Needs a boundary value");
        }
        String boundary = headerContentType[1].substring(pos + 1);
        if (boundary.charAt(0) == '"') {
            String bound = boundary.trim();
            int index = bound.length() - 1;
            if (bound.charAt(index) == '"') {
                boundary = bound.substring(1, index);
            }
        }
        multipartDataBoundary = "--" + boundary;
```

My implementation is pretty much a substring() too (2 actually).  The routine is reproduced below:

``` java
public static String[] splitOnce(String value, char delim) {
        final int delimIndex = value.indexOf(delim);

        // delim wasn't found or it was the last character so return the entire value
        if (delimIndex == -1) {
            return new String[] { value };
        }

        // delim was at the end so just put the first part into the array
        if  (delimIndex == value.length() - 1) {
           return new String[] { value.substring(0, delimIndex) };
        }

        return new String[] { value.substring(0, delimIndex), value.substring(delimIndex + 1) };
    }
```

Yes, your solution is more efficient but I don't think the above is too far off.   I defer to your better judgement.  As long as it gets fixed! :)
